  "labelNotes": "Supply: ROC prints 'IN voltage range' 4.35-26 V and 'IN operating voltage range' 4.35-6.4 V ('72/'73/'75/'79) and 4.35-10.2 V ('74). The three 4.35 V minimums collapse to one label (part-number variants are not allowed condition keys). Quiescent: IBAT(PDWN) sleep current 4.3/6.5 uA (TJ = 85 C printed in its multi-line test-condition cell), IIN standby at VIN 6 V and 10 V, ICC active supply 1.1/1.5 mA at VIN = 6 V; TYP/MAX columns confirmed with pdftotext. Abs max: all three VI Input Voltage rows (IN 28 V, BAT 5 V, OUT/EN1/EN2/CE/... 7 V). The 7 V value sits on a dump line holding only '\u20130.3 | 7 | V' (the pin list is on the lines around it), so its citation is the cell '\u20130.3', which also matches the IN and BAT lines. Excluded: abs-max II input current 1.6 A, ROC currents, ISC/IBIAS/INTC source currents, RILIM/RISET/RITERM/RTMR programming resistors (not pull-ups). EN1/EN2/CE input currents are not on the selected pages."
